{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "1b240c66-06bb-443f-9fef-7f795416b7dc",
    "name": "tamagotchi-service",
    "description": "Tamagotchi creation, stats, primary choice, XP and ownership transfer.\n\nOwner: dan1el50. Port: 8083 (reached through the gateway on 8080).\n\nEverything goes through the API Gateway (`{{gatewayUrl}}`): players register and log in at User Management through it, and the gateway verifies their token and forwards requests with `X-User-Id` + `X-Gateway-Key` instead. Battle (`xp`, `transfer-owner`) and Monster Raid (`GET /tamagotchis/{id}`) call with their `X-Service-Key` and no token. The service accepts nothing else - the `... without the gateway` request shows the 401. Each run registers new players (`{{runId}}`), so it can be run repeatedly.\n\nStat updates are checked against the package's stat definitions in Package Registry (through the gateway), so the setup folder registers a real package. Package Registry's admin is seeded by user id (PACKAGE_REGISTRY_INITIAL_ADMIN_USER_ID, `admin-1`), which no gateway login can be, so that one folder calls Package Registry directly and plays the gateway.\n\nSet these to the values in your .env (the defaults match .env.example): `{{gatewayKey}}` = GATEWAY_KEY, `{{battleServiceKey}}` = SERVICE_KEY_BATTLE, `{{monsterRaidServiceKey}}` = SERVICE_KEY_MONSTER_RAID. With newman: `--env-var gatewayKey=<key>` and so on.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "38273956"
  },
